.TH VMTOUCH 8
.SH NAME
vmtouch \- inspect, warm, evict, or lock filesystem cache pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vmtouch
.RI [ options ] " path " ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without an operation flag,
.B vmtouch
reports how many pages of the selected files are resident.
Directories are traversed recursively. The walk skips symbolic links,
crosses filesystem boundaries, and counts hardlinked files once per run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-t
Warm the selected pages by reading one byte per page.
.TP
.B \-e
Ask the operating system to evict the selected pages.
Eviction is advisory and is not guaranteed.
.TP
.B \-l
Warm and lock selected mappings with
.BR mlock (2).
The process stays running to keep its locks.
.TP
.B \-L
Warm and retain the selected mappings, then lock current process mappings
with
.BR mlockall (2).
The process stays running to keep its locks.
.TP
.BI \-m " size"
Skip files larger than
.IR size .
.TP
.BI \-p " range"
Select part of each file. Use
.IR size ,
.IR start\-end ,
or
.IR start\- .
Sizes are in bytes, with optional K, M, or G suffixes for powers of 1024.
The starting offset is rounded down to a page boundary.
.TP
.BI \-b " file"
Read paths from a batch file, or use
.B \-
for standard input.
.TP
.B \-0
Use NUL rather than newline separators in batch input.
.TP
.B \-d
Run in the background. Requires
.B \-l
or
.BR \-L .
.TP
.B \-w
With
.BR \-d ,
wait for the child to report startup success or failure.
.TP
.BI \-P " file"
Write a pidfile for a locking run. The process removes it when handling
SIGINT, SIGTERM, or SIGQUIT; it cannot clean up after SIGKILL.
.TP
.B \-o kv
Print machine-readable key=value summary fields.
.TP
.B \-v
Print aggregate output, without per-file residency charts.
.TP
.B \-q
Suppress warnings and the summary. Fatal diagnostics still go to standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the operation completed, possibly with warnings for individual
files. One means invalid usage or a fatal failure. Without
.BR \-w ,
a daemon-launching parent does not wait for the child's outcome.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mincore (2),
.BR mlock (2),
.BR mlockall (2),
.BR posix_fadvise (2)
